---
import ReferenceLayout from '../layouts/ReferenceLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';
import { href } from '../lib/url';
---
<ReferenceLayout
  title="About"
  description="RadMage Finance is a free financial education site from RadMage Labs: interactive lessons and calculators that show their formulas, with source-linked financial news in development."
  lead="RadMage Finance is a free financial education site. It explains how money, banking and interest work through interactive lessons, calculators that show their formulas, and sources you can check. A news section with headlines from named sources is in development and not live yet."
  updated="2026-11-16"
  schemaType="AboutPage"
>
  <h2>Who it is for</h2>
  <p>
    Adults in the United States who want to understand their own money and the system it
    moves through: savers comparing accounts, borrowers and homeowners looking at a loan,
    and anyone curious about how banks and the Federal Reserve actually work.
  </p>
  <p>
    No financial background is assumed. Each topic starts with a plain explanation, and the
    technical detail, including the accounting and the formulas, is there for readers who
    want it.
  </p>

  <h2>What you will find</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><a href={href('news/')}>News</a>, in development and not live yet: headlines from named publishers on markets, the economy, the Federal Reserve, banking, crypto and regulation, grouped by topic and linked to the original reporting.</li>
    <li><a href={href('learn/')}>Learn</a>: interactive lessons on what money is, how it flows between households, businesses, banks, the government and the Federal Reserve, and how banks create money when they lend.</li>
    <li><a href={href('calculators/')}>Calculators</a>: compound interest, APR and APY, high-yield savings, loan amortization and mortgage payoff.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What it is not</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Not investment advice, and not a trading-signal service.</li>
    <li>Not a recommendation of any bank, product or asset.</li>
    <li>Not a partisan outlet or a promoter of cryptocurrencies.</li>
    <li>Not a forecast: simulations are teaching models, and they are labeled as such.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How it is made</h2>
  <p>
    Facts link to their sources, preferably primary ones, with the date they were last
    checked. Each section says what kind of claim it makes, so a fact, an accounting identity,
    a simplified model, an interpretation, a calculator's projection and a forecast are never
    confused. Calculations are checked against an independent reference implementation, and
    against regulators' published worked examples where they exist. The
    details are on the <a href={href('methodology/')}>Methodology</a> page.
  </p>

  <h2>Publisher</h2>
  <p>
    RadMage Finance is published by <a href={SITE.publisherUrl}>{SITE.publisher}</a>. It is
    free to use, needs no account, and does not track you.
    Found an error? See <a href={href('corrections/')}>Corrections</a>.
  </p>
</ReferenceLayout>
